docs/modules/ROOT/pages/upgrade.adoc:46:Methods that access VM state must satisfy the SDK's `HostAccess` bounds. The public `StorageSlot::get_slot` helper also takes a VM-accessible context as its first argument: call `StorageSlot::get_slot(self, slot)` from a contract method. EIP-712 `chain_id` and `contract_address` hooks are instance methods in the new API and should read those values from `self.vm()`.
docs/modules/ROOT/pages/upgrade.adoc:54:SDK 0.10.5 deprecated the `reentrant` feature and entrypoint guard. High-level `call`, `delegate_call`, and `static_call` persist cached storage before handing control to another contract; this prevents stale storage reads during callbacks but does not replace checks-effects-interactions. SDK 0.10.10 still has the guard enabled unless the `reentrant` feature is enabled. The library forwards that feature for contracts whose external callbacks need to call back into the same contract. The flash-mint example enables it by default because borrower callbacks commonly read or call the lender token during the loan. Keep the feature only while targeting SDK versions that still have the guard; it is deprecated upstream.
docs/modules/ROOT/pages/upgrade.adoc:59:openzeppelin-stylus = { version = "0.4", features = ["reentrant"] }
docs/modules/ROOT/pages/upgrade.adoc:62:The feature does not make arbitrary reentrant logic safe. Review every external call and state invariant. `RawCall` does not flush cached storage automatically. If a raw call can reenter and read state written earlier in the current call, call `.clear_storage_cache()` on the `RawCall` before invoking it; this persists dirty values and drops the in-memory cache.
docs/modules/ROOT/pages/upgrade.adoc:72:The old `motsu` unit-test framework and this repository's `e2e` / `e2e-proc` crates were removed. For storage-only unit tests, enable `stylus-sdk`'s `stylus-test` feature and construct a fresh `TestVM` per contract under test. Set sender, contract address, block values, storage, and mocked host calls on that VM. A second `TestVM` is an independent host; it does not automatically become a deployed external contract.
docs/modules/ROOT/pages/upgrade.adoc:114:* Replace `stylus_sdk::msg`, `block`, and `contract` global accessors with `self.vm()` methods. Functions that need VM state now take `&self` or `&mut self` and satisfy the SDK `HostAccess` bounds.
docs/modules/ROOT/pages/upgrade.adoc:115:* Add the VM and a `Call` context to generated `sol_interface!` calls. Use `Call::new()` for read-only calls and `Call::new_mutating(self)` for state-changing calls.
